[Music]  boomba is an iconic character within  Dragonball and one of the most well  known characters across the planet there  are tons of people that identify Bulma  as a beacon of female empowerment and  others who disagree I happen to fall  somewhere in the middle and honestly I'm  only interested in discussing her role  as it's written within the story the  Japanese anime industry has enjoyed a  long history of success and worldwide  acclaim for the most part but something  I've always kept an eye out for while  watching and reading these series has  been their female characters and how  they fit within the story many often  times reduced to rather cliche and  boring things such as eye candy someone  to save or as someone's affection to be  one now I understand that this is an  incredibly divisive topic and simply by  the nature of it will be incredibly  personal to a lot of people despite my  best efforts to groan and focus this  video analysis in narrative theory with  that said while I will largely be  speaking from a story perspective I will  be giving opinions on the topic here and  there when it's needed to further the  discussion I'm not looking to infer  anything about who she might be as a  person just what she offers the series  as it's written by Akira Toriyama  the very same way I looked at Jordans  imasu I want to see how her character  has served the plot today I will be  dissecting and analyzing one of the  oldest and most iconic female characters  to come out of Japan today I will be  breaking down the brash the beautiful  and the genius Bulma  [Music]  I really like Bulma as a character I'm  sure there are nostalgic reasons that  play in my mind to create this opinion  but from a narrative point of view as a  personality I think she's easily one of  the most standout and memorable in the  series for better or worse and whatever  your opinion of her it's impossible to  deny that you know exactly what she's  like even if you've only had limited  exposure to her and that's terrific  characterization with that said I do  have some critiques the first being  would have the most common throughout  fiction and that is that she's  essentially a plot device now I know  that implies she's a husk of a character  made to fulfill a specific function  within the story and while she is much  more than that both for great and  terrible reasons which I'll get to later  I do think that she is a plot device  within the show in fact I'd even go as  far as to say that she is primarily a  plot device by design but I'm getting a  little ahead of myself here  what's a plot device in storytelling the  goal is to move from one key moment to  the next as seamlessly as possible until  the conclusion of the narrative has been  reached oftentimes the story's  characters can get into circumstances  that brings the stories forward momentum  to a screeching halt and so if we keep  that in mind a plot device is an object  or character in the story whose purpose  is purely to drive the plot forward  maintaining its flow or resolving  situations within it it could be  something everybody wants to obtain a  device that must be destroyed or an  annoying teenager who must be protected  at all costs I did not write this  definition I found it online and it's as  if it was written specifically to make  the point that Bulma fits the role  perfectly at the very beginning of the  story she is the character that  introduces Goku the main character to  the Dragon Balls and the wider world  through the use of her intelligence and  gadgets she bridges the gaps in the plot  were necessary transporting our heroes  and solving the problems the plot  produces such as space traversing and  even time travel she is also quite often  the subject of multiple kidnappings and  countless rescues now can a character be  a plot device and compelling at the same  time well yeah absolutely  Walter White being a chemistry teacher  is in some form a plot device that  enables the story being told to flow  comfortably however in his case he is a  great character first and a plot device  second so what makes a great female  character this  is a question that's getting asked more  and more frequently in recent years as  we strive for less would note female  characters and honestly it's a strange  one to me the answer to what makes a  good female character is the exact same  as what makes a good character period  now the answer to this isn't exactly  easy to pin down but in general if you  want to twist my arm for a definition a  good character to me at least is one  that breeds interest within the story  they exist Walter White is a compelling  character that emphasizes the best  attributes of Breaking Bad  god damn right eren yeager facilitates  the most interesting outcomes in attack  on Titan Goku is a perfect catalyst for  wonderful things to happen in Dragon  Ball and awful things to happen in  Dragon Ball super yeah yeah yeah yes so  what did bulla bring to the table for  this story well a friend of mine took  time to ask a few of her friends and  other female Dragon Ball fans in the  community what their take was on the  character this is what they had to say  at the beginning Bulma Zoli motivation  was to have a boyfriend she was willing  to use her looks to get what she wanted  while manipulating those around her she  was incredibly capable and still is  proving herself proficient with tech  more so than any other character which  was interesting because in a show that  revolves around guys that rely on their  physical prowess to get ahead how can a  female role come into play that isn't  just the strong girl characters like  Vidal and chichi began as fighters or  physically strong characters within the  story but sort of lost relevancy within  the narrative due to lack of utility  bull de never had such a problem which  is sort of interesting because back in  the early 80s when this story was  written in both the west and the east  female characters were very much prizes  to be won by the hero mild-mannered  SWE's and in a lot of ways helpless so  for the time that she was introduced  boomers character having any edge to her  at all with any abilities was in many  ways a win in the direction of strong  female character writing she doesn't  want nor has she ever wanted a  stereotypical life she might have wanted  in the beginning to get a cute boyfriend  but it's a selfish desire of hers and  changing her mind on that was the arc  her character underwent in the beginning  chichi and Videl both get pregnant and  seemed to solely focus on their kids and  lose a lot of what made their characters  have more of that focus in the story  originally we  was their ability to face however since  Pumas strength lies with her smarts and  her sexuality  she doesn't have to necessarily give  that up as much after becoming a mother  I mean boomers showing up in the Android  saga as a single mother was a massive  deal that's not a thing that's done in  Japan and certainly wasn't back then and  that's just one aspect of boomers  character people can relate to even  today a lot of female fans who love  Dragon Ball Z as a teen have to deal  with what she's experiencing right now -  we're all getting older some of us have  kids and despite it being played for  laughs  when the brouilly movie and even battle  of gods drew attention to boomers aging  I was honestly amazed because you never  talk about aging in Japan there's a  saying there about women who are  Christmas cakes no one wants you after  the 25th meaning if you're not married  by 25 your scene is past your prime  honestly there's a lot to be said about  sexuality and its use in media and of  course each culture has its own unique  sexuality issues and morals Japan just  happens to have some of the most  interesting concerning sexuality and you  have to take into account the lingering  dampening effects of a less progressive  and more traditional Society of which  Japan while definitely making progress  is still very much operating under is  boma still used as a sex object  of course her body is always on display  and with her sexuality and appearance  being part of her strength aging from a  narrative point of view is an  interesting part of her plotline which  is something about her character I would  love to see come more into play as the  show continues the guys in the show get  to stay the same for the most part their  strength only expands but the very area  boma relied on to give her some of her  strength her body as an object of desire  is now aging and how she deals with that  could be really interesting seeing as we  never got to see that for me personally  the story should always come first an  easing extra should be left out if a  character isn't serving a purpose by  conducting themselves it has seen the  way that they are it only serves to  bring the story down this is why I'm not  a fan of fanservice others love it and  many are different to it I think there's  a time and place for everything and from  the shows I've seen very few choose  their moments tastefully the most  irritating part about this for me is  what could have been bull muff from  Future Trunks as timeline has a story  more interesting than that  which we got from black and Zuma sue got  an emotional level at least anyway in  her troubled timeline her genius is the  most valuable trait as it's the only one  that can bring about victory which plays  into the Dragon Ball formula of  progression through struggle her  struggling to get the parts and feel  necessary to travel back in time to  change the fate of that timeline and to  maybe see the person she loves one more  time that's a compelling emotional story  that wasn't touched on nearly enough in  the original koku black arc or even in  the Android saga it wasn't brought up at  all in the anime and was only briefly  touched on during Toyota Rose manga you  have a character that's understood by  the audience  intimately and you never utilized them  to their fullest potential now I'm not  suggesting an arc centred around boomers  antics by any means but she definitely  had more to add to that story than that  which was shown and I honestly think a  lot was left on the table that wasn't  embraced look my intention for this  video is not to act as yet another  mindless voice talking about  representation into the void of the  internet and I'm definitely not someone  that thinks people can't think for  themselves because a movie or TV show  tells them or doesn't tell them how to  feel but instead this video was made to  offer to the best of my abilities an  explanation as to where I think and  others think there are opportunities  being norge and aspects that deserve  appreciation opportunities for better  and more emotionally rich stories that  make the most of their characters I  personally want opportunities for better  and more emotionally rich stories that  make the most of all of their characters  and honestly there are very few  characters as real and is fully realized  as Bulma in asking around for opinions  on her character one aspect offer that  many ladies mentioned was how real she  felt in a show full of people who  literally couldn't be real here she is a  very real human being as flawed and  emotional as any of us almost anyone  else in the main story has something  about them that could never actually  occur three eyes their strength tails  sneezing related mental disorders flying  I suppose one could say that inventing  capsule technology is not real and yeah  I guess I see that but the idea behind  that advantage is knowledge and  technology those are real things if I  wanted to I could try and become as  proficient an engineer as she is  supposed to be but no matter how hard  anyone  they will never be able to achieve what  Goku has heck even Vegeta can't do it  and he's as unbelievable as he is so I  asked are we getting the most emotional  stories from bulma's character that we  can know most definitely not is there  perhaps a lack of enthusiasm from Japan  to push in this direction I would  personally think so and I think that's  the biggest problem many female  characters and fans of those characters  have trouble with today however despite  this there's certainly no denying that  bullet is a fantastic character with  arguably just as much if not more  personality than any other character in  the series which is why I wanted to  write this video in the first place all  the stories that could have been told  but never were and some that we  hopefully might hear in the not so  distant future thanks for watching  [Music]

